C3
[END]

Simple DIFS formula that (using pseudorandom numbers) generates an uniform
pattern of cubes on XY plane. Vtn values near to zero may be a little noisy on edges due to
some simplifications I made.

Two different kinds of shapes can be gnerated at the same time!
You can choose different shape variations if you change Shape types;
0 = Rectangular prisms
1 = Cones (or cylinders)
2 = Spheres (or cylinders)
3 = Pyramids (in this case you can use Vtn > 1 for less sharp solids)
4 = Solid arcs
5 = Tubey arcs
6 = Rounded square prisms
7 = Prisms of cylinders (like CubeTubeIFS)
8 = Intersecting circle/square prisms
9 = Intersecting circle/hexagonal prisms
10 = Hexagonal-base Pyramids
11 = Octagonal/square prisms
12 = Water-top prisms          (a bit slow)
13 = Water-top curvy solids    (slower than previous)
14 = Curvy solids              (slower than previous)
15 = Gumdrop toruses
16 = Spheres on cylindrical legs
17 = Cubes on cylindrical legs
18 = Cylindrical legs (pyramid) - Note: 
XVtn controls the base of each pyramid, when close to 1 they
are allowed to degenerate into an infinite tube.
19 = Pointy-rounded pyramids


Luca GN 2012/2016